      "turn": 15,
      "tool": "add_note",
      "args": {
        "text": "The anchor room. A Japandi living room seen straight on from the doorway, eye height. Left: a wall of shoji screens, morning light through the paper. Centre: a low, long three-seat sofa in oatmeal linen on thin oak legs; in front of it a low rectangular solid-oak coffee table with one stoneware bowl. Right: two Wishbone-style oak chairs with paper-cord seats, and an Akari-style washi floor lamp. Floor: pale oak boards with a flat-woven wool rug. Back wall: warm white lime plaster with one low oak sideboard. Palette: natural blonde wood, oatmeal, warm white, one charcoal accent. No clutter, no pattern, no gloss. Photographic, natural daylight."
      },
      "say": "Writing the anchor room: the bones from the Japanese references, the furniture from the Danish ones. Every later variation keeps this exact layout.",
      "ok": true,
